Annadaan Connect

About the Project
Annadaan Connect is a food sharing platform designed to reduce food waste and address hunger in communities across India. The name "Annadaan" comes from the Sanskrit term for "food donation," a concept deeply rooted in Indian culture as a form of charity and goodwill.
This platform connects people who have excess food with those who need it, offering both free donation options and "pay what you can" models to maintain dignity and accessibility.
Show Image
Features
For Food Donors

Create listings for excess food (home-cooked meals, restaurant surplus, groceries)
Choose between free donations or set a flexible price
Earn karma points for every donation
Track impact through a personal dashboard
Redeem karma points for partner rewards

For Food Recipients

Browse food listings by location and preferences
Option to get food for free or pay what you can
Anonymous pickup options for dignity preservation
Rate and thank donors
Become donors themselves in the future

Community Features

Location-based matching system
In-app messaging for coordination
Review and rating system
Community recognition for regular donors
Social sharing to spread awareness

Technology Stack
Backend

Java 17
Spring Boot 2.7.0
Spring Security for authentication
Spring Data JPA for database operations
H2 Database (development) / MySQL (production)
RESTful API architecture

Frontend

HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript
Bootstrap 5 for responsive design
Custom animations with GSAP
Form validation with JavaScript
Interactive maps for location services

Setup Instructions
Prerequisites

JDK 17 or higher
Maven 3.8+
MySQL (for production deployment)
IDE with Spring support (IntelliJ IDEA recommended)

Local Development Setup

Clone the repository
bashgit clone https://github.com/yourusername/annadaan-connect.git
cd annadaan-connect

Build the project
bashmvn clean install

Run the application
bashmvn spring-boot:run
The application will be available at http://localhost:8080
Database Setup

The application uses H2 in-memory database by default for development
For production, update application.properties with your MySQL credentials



Configuration
Key configuration files:

application.properties: Main application configuration
data.sql: Initial data setup (sample users, listings)

Project Structure
annadaan-connect/
├── src/
│   ├── main/
│   │   ├── java/com/annadaan/
│   │   │   ├── controllers/    # API endpoints and page controllers
│   │   │   ├── models/         # Entity classes
│   │   │   ├── repositories/   # Data access interfaces
│   │   │   ├── services/       # Business logic
│   │   │   ├── config/         # Configuration classes
│   │   │   └── AnnadaanConnectApplication.java
│   │   │
│   │   └── resources/
│   │       ├── static/         # Static resources (CSS, JS, images)
│   │       ├── templates/      # Thymeleaf templates
│   │       └── application.properties
│   │
│   └── test/                   # Unit and integration tests
│
├── pom.xml                     # Maven dependencies
└── README.md
